// Cardnull OS 2 — the seed kernel.
//
// Stone 1: first boot. This program is compiled with
// `niflac --bare` into a binary that boots on its own — no
// operating system underneath it. It clears nothing and owns
// everything: it greets the person in plain words, says how
// much memory the machine has (the loader's memory map, read
// with memorysize()), and then stays alive, sleeping between
// timer ticks — the tick has been running since the machine
// woke, and Stone 2 will let a person hear it.
//
// The screen is the text screen; `say` writes there, line by
// line, and scrolls when it must.

say "Cardnull"
say "Welcome. This computer is yours, and everything on it is given freely."
say "This machine has " + memorysize() + " bytes of memory (" + (memorysize() / 1048576) + " megabytes)."

// An operating system does not exit. Sleep a tick at a time,
// forever; the timer interrupt keeps the count while we rest.
while true {
    waittick()
}
